  "description": "The meme frames Lizzie Velasquez as an inspirational figure solely because of her perceived 'overcoming' of her rare genetic condition, reducing her value to her resilience rather than her individuality. This trope is expressed through the text overlay and the visual presentation of her as a motivational speaker, which may unintentionally or intentionally reinforce societal stigma around physical difference and imply her value is derived solely from her resilience rather than her humanity. This can be seen as a form of ableism, as it reduces her to a symbol of inspiration for others' suffering, potentially reinforcing societal stigma around physical difference and implying her value is derived solely from her resilience rather than her individuality.",
